; A `Key: value` comment sets a tag only when the key is the comment's
; first whitespace-delimited token of two or more characters.  A later
; token never names a key; a one-character token before it is skipped;
; a leading `:tag:` token takes the first position, so no key follows.
; The `Key:: expr` form follows the same rule.

2024/01/01 First token is the key
    ; Key: alpha
    Expenses:Food    $1.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 Later token is not a key
    ; foo Key: beta
    Expenses:Food    $2.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/03 One-character tokens are skipped
    ; - Key: gamma
    Expenses:Food    $3.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/04 A tag token ends the key position
    ; :urgent: Key: delta
    Expenses:Food    $4.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/05 Value expressions follow the same rule
    ; - Key:: 2 + 3
    Expenses:Food    $5.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/06 A later value expression is not a key
    ; foo Key:: 2 + 3
    Expenses:Food    $6.00
    Assets:Cash

test reg Food --format '%(payee) [%(tag("Key"))] [%(has_tag("urgent"))]\n'
First token is the key [alpha] [false]
Later token is not a key [] [false]
One-character tokens are skipped [gamma] [false]
A tag token ends the key position [] [true]
Value expressions follow the same rule [5] [false]
A later value expression is not a key [] [false]
end test
